                    <td class="doc-td">2</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><input type="checkbox"> model+item</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><input type="checkbox"> queued</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Note:</strong> qty shown is the count of manual mentions, not final
            print qty — confirm against the BOM when creating items. Door/spool parts use their own 3MF.
            Preview images are distinct per source file (top_N.png); they are plate thumbnails, not the
            individual part mesh — match the code to the manual page before printing.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="hardware-worksheet" class="doc-h2">5c. Hardware (purchased) parts worksheet</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">These are the <strong>BUY, not print</strong> components from the HDRY assembly
            manual (DryerProjectPlan section 1b / import pack). Each row is <strong>general stock</strong> (any BOM can use it), <code>item_origin=purchased</code>.
            The dryer BASE/MOD BOMs attach these later; the SKU is not dryer-prefixed. Wheel hardware is per wheel (4 wheels per base unit).
            Multi-supplier: the PO / todo (#2310) must support an item mapping to several suppliers
            (InventoryItemSupplier). Docs first — rows below are the source of truth for inventory creation.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">SKU</th><th class="doc-th">Name</th><th class="doc-th">Qty / unit</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">UoM</th><th class="doc-th">Category</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Reorder min</th><th class="doc-th">Reorder qty (order unit)</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-M4-14</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">M4x14 screw</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">180</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_fastener</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">180</td><td class="doc-td">200 (box)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-M3-20</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">M3x20 screw</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">16</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_fastener</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">16</td><td class="doc-td">100 (bag)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-608ZZ</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">608zz bearing</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">16</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_bearing</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">16</td><td class="doc-td">20 (set)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-MAG-8X2</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">8x2 mm magnet</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">20</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_magnet</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">20</td><td class="doc-td">50 (pack)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-GASKET-6X3</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Adhesive gasket</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">6</td><td class="doc-td">m</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_gasket</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">6</td><td class="doc-td">6 (roll) / 30 (roll)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-POLYDRYER</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Polydryer</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">1</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_consumable</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">1</td><td class="doc-td">1 (unit)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-WASHER</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Washer (wheel)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">8 (4-8/wheel x4)</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_fastener</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">8</td><td class="doc-td">100 (bag)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-BOLT-NUT</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Bolt + nut (wheel)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">8 (4-8/wheel x4)</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_fastener</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">8</td><td class="doc-td">100 (bag)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>HW-SPACER-50</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">50 mm spacer (wheel)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">8 (4-8/wheel x4)</td><td class="doc-td">each</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">hardware_spacer</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">8</td><td class="doc-td">50 (pack)</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Reorder rule (hardware rows):</strong>
            <code>reorder_point</code> (min) = qty needed for one base unit; <code>reorder_quantity</code> =
            common order unit (box / bag / set / roll shown). For the printed parts (section 5b) the rule
            flips: <code>reorder_quantity</code> = qty needed per build config, not a wholesale unit.
            All hardware rows: <code>show_in_shop=0</code>, <code>list_in_marketplace=0</code>.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Created via the live Inventory UI (/Inventory/item/add) under sitename=3d;
            BOM lines added under INT-HDRY-001 (base unit) and the later add-on module parent. Tracked by
            todo #2309; PO for these rows is blocking todo #2310 (multi-supplier aware).</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>
